{
  "repo": "microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat",
  "number": 6009,
  "title": "Announce \"Sending message.\" when a message takes over 3 seconds to send",
  "body": "> Fixes #5700. Continues #5781 by @isherstneva, with @compulim's rework.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed [#5700](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/issues/5700), screen readers not announcing that a message is still being sent, in PR [#6009](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/6009), by [@isherstneva](https://github.com/isherstneva), [@compulim](https://github.com/compulim), and [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nScreen readers said nothing while a message was still being sent, such as a slow upload (the issue is closed, but no release fixes it). Now the live region announces \"Sending message.\" once after 3 seconds of sending; faster sends stay silent.\n\n## Design\n\n- Once until nothing is sending, not every 3 seconds as in #5781's last commit: other announcements are said once, and an attachment (120-second timeout) would be announced up to 39 times.\n- `useIsSending()` stays internal (`botframework-webchat-api/internal.js`) until a host needs it. A `role=\"status\"` on the visible \"Sending\" would announce every send at once.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `ActivitySendStatusComposer`: `useIsSending()`, true while a visible activity is sending; `isPresentational` moved to core\n- `LongSend`: announces \"Sending message.\" once after 3 seconds of sending, also via `ariaNotify()`\n- `SendFailed`: skips failed sends without an activity\n- `activityStatus.longSend.html`: fake clock; snapshots 1–3, nothing at 2.999 s, announced at 3 s, still once after the ack\n- `.fast`, `.sendFailed`, `.event`: snapshot 1, nothing for an ack at 2.999 s, a failure, an event\n- `.language`: snapshot 1, a text change does not announce again, the next send uses the new text\n- `ariaNotify/longSend.html`: announced once via `ariaNotify()`\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [ ] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n\n",
